p: .
t. 
|  The involvement of auxiliaries dramatically changes the landscape of
|  custody/abuse litigation. When a mother makes an abuse allegation that
|  is not supported by social workers, for instance, she finds herself fighting
|  not only against one adversary (her ex-husband) but against an array of
|  other actors who may then lend considerable official support (free of
.  charge) to the mother’s adversary


