|  First, the proceedings are confidential. This protects family court
|  judges from the restraining influence of the public eye. In some states
|  family courts are closed by statute; in other states, at least in theory,
|  an evidentiary hearing must take place to determine if the case should
|  be closed. But, in practice, judges can easily seal court records and close
|  hearings to the public. This gives family courts unusual leeway in threat-
|  ening or punishing litigants without anyone outside the court being any
.  the wiser


--- Sentence/switch
